What is a Request for Bank or Credit Reference?
A Request for Bank or Credit Reference is a formal document used by lenders, businesses, landlords, or creditors to obtain financial background information before granting a loan or extending credit.
This document helps verify whether an applicant has responsibly managed past loans, bank accounts, or credit obligations. It can reduce lending risk and support better financial decisions.

________________________________________

Why Use a Request for Bank or Credit Reference?
Using a properly drafted Request for Bank or Credit Reference helps:
• Check creditworthiness before lending money
• Verify banking relationships
• Review repayment history
• Reduce risk of loan default
• Support credit approval decisions
• Build trust in business transactions
• Create formal documentation records

